          "title": "You'll want to know: प्रत्यागच्छति",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "प्रत्यागच्छति — pratyāgacchati — \"comes back, returns\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "pratyāgacchati is built from prati \"back, against\", ā \"toward\" and the root √gam \"go\", whose present stem is gaccha- (MW): \"comes back, returns\". It is āgacchati \"comes\" with prati in front, and MW sets √gam beside English come."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
